ct. Usually, this means the object shouldn't dominate. But in the context of 'EDITORIAL HERO: wide high-oblique... remain small', 50% is NOT small. It is large. Therefore, I should reject based on width.", "I will check the strict 'Hard Reject' criteria again. The width is clearly >25%. The prompt says 'Hard reject a pair wider than 25 percent'. Therefore, Pass = false.", 'machine-enforced bounding-box check failed: Reduce the product group from 52% to 8-25% of frame width.']
